From: Keith Carter <oss@keithbcarter.com>
Subject: [PATCH v2 for 0.7] ipa: simple: agc: Honor ExposureValue control and tuning-file default

The simple soft-ISP AGC drives the histogram Mean Sample Value (MSV) to a
fixed target (kExposureOptimal, the middle of the range). On sensors whose
output tends to over-expose, this clips the brightest highlights: on the
OV5675 (MSI Prestige 13 A2VMG) bright white fabric clips the green channel
first and the clipped pixels tint pink/magenta. There is currently no way
to bias the AGC target: the ExposureValue control is advertised by the
control API but silently ignored by this IPA.

Make the simple AGC honor the ExposureValue control by scaling the optimal
MSV target by 2^EV (the documented log2 semantic), clamped to the valid MSV
range. EV=0 preserves the previous behaviour exactly. Additionally, allow a
per-sensor default bias to be supplied in the tuning file ("exposureValue"
in the Agc block) so that consumers which never set the control still get a
sensible exposure for that sensor. A runtime ExposureValue control overrides
the tuning-file default. The current value is reported in metadata.

Signed-off-by: Keith Carter <oss@keithbcarter.com>
---
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.h
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.h
@@ -19,6 +19,11 @@
 	Agc();
 	~Agc() = default;
 
